## Exercise 1: make the design object {.smaller}

Follow along: [Exercises template](Exercises/Exercises.qmd){target="_blank"} | [Solutions](Exercises/Solutions.qmd){target="_blank"}.

Use `ess_der` and {srvyr} to create a survey design object called `ess_des`. The ESS design variables are:

- `psu`: primary sampling unit (cluster)
- `stratum`: stratum
- `anweight`: analysis weight

Remember that some `psu` codes repeat across different `stratum` values.

```{r}
#| label: 06-happy-design-obj-exercise
#| echo: false
#| class-output: scroll-output
ess_des <- ess_der |>
  as_survey_design(
    ids = psu,
    strata = stratum,
    weights = anweight,
    nest = TRUE
  )

ess_des
```

